  "gaps": [
    "Per-course credits for MAT2051 and the core, specialization, and IT4997 courses are not printed beside the course names. The two-column PDF extraction scattered them. They were reconstructed from the order of the stray credit numbers and confirmed against the printed block minimums: core at least 54 (IT2230 and PM1000 at 3, the others at 6), specialization at least 30, capstone at least 12. They should be verified against the source PDF.",
    "The 33-credit remaining general education block is derived, not printed. The capture states 45 general education quarter credits that include the required courses MAT1050 and MAT2051 (12 credits). The 45 total is also implied by 45 + 54 + 30 + 39 + 12 = 180.",
    "The general education block requires at least 4 quarter credits from each category (Communication, Humanities, Natural Science and Mathematics, Social Science). The category-level breakdown of the remaining 33 credits is left to student choice and is not itemized.",
    "Program minimum of 54 quarter credits at the 3000 level and above is a constraint not represented as a separate ledger line.",
    "An optional Honors Pathway (PHI-H2005 3, COM-H4005 6, SOC-H3005 6; at least 15 quarter credits) applies toward general education for honors students only. It is not included in the standard ledger.",
    "The capture states no residency or institutional-credit requirement (courses that must be completed at Capella). Transfer credit limits are also not stated.",
    "Capstone courses must be taken during the student's final two quarters. Prerequisites are referenced but not detailed in the capture."
  ],
